{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 46.6% a year from $6.91 billion in FY2017 to $215.9 billion in FY2026 [F1][F10][F211]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was not smooth: FY2020 fell 6.8% and FY2023 grew only 0.2%, while FY2024 and FY2025 rose 125.9% and 114.2% [D130][D284][D338][D393]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2024 step change came from Data Center revenue up 217%, driven by Hopper GPU shipments for LLM training and inference [P22][P23]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2026 growth of 65.5% was driven by Blackwell data center compute and networking, with Data Center networking up 142% [D448][P8][P10]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Data Center was 89.7% of FY2026 revenue and contributed 60.2pp of the 65.5% growth [D620][D622][D448]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Within it, Compute contributed 46.1pp and Networking 14.1pp in FY2026 [D629][D636]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The filing attributes the increase to accelerated computing and AI platform shifts, with Blackwell the majority of Data Center revenue [P8][P10]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 60.1% against 65.5% revenue growth, an incremental margin of 57.3% [D449][D448][D475]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS rose 66.7% against 64.7% net income growth as the diluted share count fell 1.2% [D452][D450][D470]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 60.4% in FY2026 sits far above the 32.8% window median and just below the 62.4% FY2025 high [F50][D813][D812]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2026 margin fell 2.0pp, with cost of revenue subtracting 3.9pp, partly offset by R&D and SG&A adding 1.3pp and 0.6pp [D463][D477][D478][D479]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The cost-of-revenue drag includes a $4.5 billion H20 excess inventory and purchase obligation charge in the first quarter [P7]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "R&D and SG&A grew on compensation, employee growth and compute infrastructure, per the filing [P5][P4][P9]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net margin of 55.6% trailed operating margin by 4.8pp, as other income of $11.1 billion partly offset a 15.1% tax rate [F70][F50][D861][X120][D434]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $102.7 billion was 0.86x net income, the window low against a 0.97x median [F100][F60][D435][D851]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow of $96.7 billion was a 44.8% margin, near the 44.4% window median [F110][D432][D822]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex of $6.04 billion was 2.8% of revenue and 2.13x D&A, up from 1.74x in FY2025 [F105][F10][D431][D437][D382]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Inventory grew 112.3% and receivables 66.8%, both faster than revenue, holding conversion below 1.0x [D474][D473][D448]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Total debt was $8.47 billion against $10.6 billion of cash in FY2026 [D440][F150]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2026 net-cash figure omits short-term investments, which were not reported that year, so the net-cash comparison across the gap is not like for like [R3]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity of 101.5% ranks at the 100th percentile of six semis peers against a 20.3% median [D447][D848][D849]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks and dividends of $41.1 billion absorbed 42.5% of free cash flow, and the share count fell 1.2% [D443][D444][D470]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Short-term investments were not reported in FY2026 though reported in FY2025, so cash and investments and net cash omit them [R3][X188]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "That data gap weakens any liquidity or net-cash conclusion drawn across the FY2025 to FY2026 boundary [R3]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Graphics was 44.1% of revenue and fell 25.0% in FY2023, a one-period cyclical drawdown [R1][D753][D754]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "That decline reflected $2.17 billion of inventory provisions on excess Ampere Gaming and Data Center supply [P35][P38]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Product revenue members sum to 190% of consolidated FY2026 revenue, so they cannot be added [R2]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin: a print below the 62.4% FY2025 high would extend the FY2026 compression, reported in the FY2027 10-K [D812][F50]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cash conversion: operating cash flow below 0.86x net income would mark a new window low, reported in the FY2027 10-K [D435]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Data Center share: a move below the 89.7% FY2026 level would signal the largest driver losing concentration, reported in the FY2027 10-K [D620]."}
  ]}
